# `COPY . .` takes everything not listed here.
#
# Two of these matter more than the rest: .venv is hundreds of megabytes of
# Windows-built packages that are useless inside a Linux image, and .env holds
# the live database URI, the JWT secret and the Stripe keys - baking it into a
# layer would ship the platform's secrets inside the image, where they survive
# every later `docker run` regardless of what the environment says.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.venv/
venv/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

.git/
.gitignore
.idea/
.vscode/

tests/
postman/
docker-compose.yml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
*.docx
README.md
start.bat

# scripts_create_superadmin.py stays in the image: it is the way back in if
# seeding is ever skipped and nobody can reach the admin area.
